  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSI₁ = 9064\n\nRate₁ = 5.5%\n\nTime₁ = 3(1)/(5) = 16/5 years\n\nRate₂ = 7.5%\n\nTime₂ = 9(3)/(5) = 48/5 years\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nSI = (P × R × T) / 100\n\nAmount = P + SI\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n9064 = (P × 5.5 × 16/5) / 100\n\n⇒ 9064 = (P × 5.5 × 16) / 500\n\n⇒ 9064 = (P × 88) / 500\n\n⇒ 9064 = P × 0.176\n\n⇒ P = 9064 ÷ 0.176\n\n⇒ P = 51500\n\nNow calculate SI₁:\n\nSI₂ = (51500 × 7.5 × 48/5) / 100\n\n⇒ SI2 = (51500 × 7.5 × 48) / 500\n\n⇒ SI2 = (51500 × 360) / 500\n\n⇒ SI2 = 51500 × 0.72\n\n⇒ SI2 = 37080\n\nAmount payable = P + SI2\n\n⇒ 51500 + 37080 = 88580\n\n**∴ Amount payable = 88,580.**\n\n12a:Tc8c",
